The computable presentation of the hint system enumerates the hint neighbourhoods, and every neighbourhood arises in this way. Equality of an intersection of two enumerated neighbourhoods with a third is the meet relation, and consistency is the consistency relation, each transported to the hint neighbourhoods by the intersection and joint-inclusion laws. The intersection function is the meet function. On a consistent pair, a lower hint neighbourhood splits into two inclusions, hence into consistency, and the meet specification together with the intersection law says that the intersection equals the hint neighbourhood of the meet index. The master index is the greatest code, whose hint neighbourhood is everything.
